# Managed by Ansible (net-openwrt role) — manual edits will be overwritten.
# fw4's input dispatch is purely iifname-based, and tailscale0 is not a
# netifd interface, so `list network 'tailscale0'` in the lan zone never
# produces a jump. Jumping input_lan does not help either — the zone's
# terminal accept re-tests iifname "br-lan", so tailnet packets would fall
# through to handle_reject. Accept directly. fw4 flushes
# and rebuilds its table on every reload, so this file is re-sourced each
# time via the `config include` stanza and cannot accumulate duplicates.
nft insert rule inet fw4 input iifname "tailscale0*" counter accept
